---
import WorkbenchScene from './WorkbenchScene.astro';
const arrow = "M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6";
---
<section class="workshop-hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="workshop-title" data-workshop-hero>
  <div class="workshop-room" role="img" aria-label="Miguel’s impedance matcher on a laboratory workbench, surrounded by its control PCB, printed schematic, connector leads and a precision driver.">
    <WorkbenchScene subject="matcher" priority opening class="workbench-occupied" />
    <WorkbenchScene subject="matcher" empty opening class="workbench-vacant" />
    <picture class="workshop-scene" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="/assets/matcher/film/landscape-machine.webp" width="1920" height="1440" alt="" loading="eager" decoding="async" />
    </picture>
  </div>
  <div class="workshop-hero-copy">
    <h1 id="workshop-title">Hardware <span>&amp; firmware.</span></h1>
    <div class="workshop-hero-intro">
      <p>I'm Miguel, an electrical &amp; computer engineer at Carnegie Mellon.</p>
      <div class="workshop-hero-actions">
        <a class="workshop-link" href="#project-matcher">Explore my work <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d={arrow} /></svg></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="workshop-hero-foot"><span class="availability-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p>Available for full-time roles<br /><strong>May 2027</strong></p></div>
  <div class="workbench-object-note" aria-hidden="true"><span>On the bench / 01</span><b>Automated RF matcher</b><span>Built for Carnegie Mellon’s Hacker Fab</span></div>
</section>
